<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 58.8 percent of their 1997/98 wheat crop by July 18, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly report Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with 79.1 percent completion of a larger sown area by the same date last season. Rain the preceding week slowed sowing again in large parts of Buenos Aires and La Pampa. Farmers had sown 108,060 hectares out of an intended 258,400 hectares of brewers barley by July 18. Farmers in Entre Rios had sown 69.1 percent of their intended 98,000 hectares of linseed. Nationally, farmers plan to sow 113,100 hectares with linseed.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,250  58.8  (79.1)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,952  100.0(100.0) 3,191.7   98.3  (97.5)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,346.9  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     805  100.0(100.0)   677.2   99.2  (99.4)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   848.4   95.7  (92.3)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
